# The page offers to install Samba itself when it is missing, so this is a
# weak dependency: the module is useful on a machine that does not have a
# file server yet, and pointless on one that never will.
Recommends: samba
Description: Cockpit module for managing Samba file shares
 A Cockpit page for managing Samba file shares: create and edit shares, give
 local accounts access to them, watch who is connected, and keep the server
 configuration in order, without leaving the web console.
 .
 Shares can be made read-only or read-write, hidden from browsing, opened to
 guests, or restricted to particular users and groups. A share whose folder is
 missing, or which SELinux is blocking, is detected and can be fixed from the
 page.
 .
 Changes are checked with testparm before they are written, the previous
 configuration is kept as a backup, and comments and settings the page does not
 manage are left untouched.
